/**
 * @file CoreServices.dox
 * @author Alexandru ALEXANDRESCU
 * @brief Doxygen documentation for the Core services: EventManager, ServiceBaseQueue, ServiceManager
 * 
 * 
 * @page ServicesTemplatesPage Services Templates Overview 
 *
 * @section Introduction
 *
 * Project CORE is a message-driven service architecture base for embedded systems.
 *
 * The basic unit of this architecture is a Service object that inherits from @ref ServiceBaseQueuePage "ServiceBaseQueue" for asyncronous multithreaded operations
 * or @ref ServiceBasePage "ServiceBase" for synchronous single thread operations.
 *
 * @section com Communication Model
 *
 * Services never call each other directly.
 * Communication is performed by publishing events to the EventManager.
 *
 * @warning All the services and the CORE are using a common set of enums from the "include_commons" folder. 
 * @warning Copy it inside your project folder, do not modify it directly. All the event types and services ids MUST extend these files !
 *
 * @section temp Templates
 *
 * To facilitate service creation a service template is provided in the deploy/templates folder or examples/templates foler internally @ref ServiceTemplatePage "Templates" .
 *
 * @section EventManager
 *
 * The EventManager is responsible for delivering events to subscribers.
 *
 * Responsibilities:
 * - Maintain subscriber lists for each EventType.
 * - Provide thread-safe event posting.
 * - Dispatch events from a dedicated dispatcher thread.
 *
 * Internally the EventManager contains:
 * - a dispatcher thread
 * - a thread-safe event queue
 * - a subscriber registry:
 *
 * @section ServiceBaseQueue
 *
 * ServiceBaseQueue is the base class for all asyncronous application services.
 *
 * Each service:
 * - has a unique ServiceId
 * - subscribes to events through the EventManager
 * - handles events via onEvent()
 *
 * Provided functionality:
 * - subscribe(EventType)
 * - unsubscribe(EventType)
 * - post events to the EventManager
 * - `run()` loop to run inside a worker thread;
 * - `init()` optional initialization method that must be called after the constructor have been called - use it for subscriptions
 * - `setup()` optional setup method executed once after start, inside the service thread - use it for initialization in the working thread !
 * - `update()` optional method executed periodically inside the worker thread.
 * - `run()` exits when `running_ == false` and queue is empty.
 * - `start()` must be called before entering `run()` loop.
 * - `stop()` signals termination and unblocks waiting threads.
 *
 * @note ServiceBaseQueue does not create threads itself. Thread ownership belongs to
 * the ServiceManager.
 * 
 * @section ServiceManager
 *
 * The ServiceManager is responsible for creating and managing services.
 *
 * Responsibilities:
 * - instantiate services
 * - start service threads
 * - stop services
 * - join service threads during shutdown
 *
 * Each service thread executes the service run loop.
 *
 * @section Lifecycle
 *
 * Startup sequence:
 * 1. Create EventManager
 * 2. Create ServiceManager
 * 3. Register services
 * 4. Start UI loop
 *
 * Shutdown sequence:
 * 1. Stop UI loop
 * 2. Stop EventManager dispatcher thread
 * 3. Stop all services
 * 4. Join service threads
 * 5. Destroy objects
 *
 * @warning The EventManager must remain alive while services may still publish events.
 * 
 *
 * @section examples Examples
 *
 * Create your service class, add it to the CMakeLists.txt sources, add the corresponding service id to the ServiceTypes.hpp 
 * and the coresponding event types to the EventTypes.hpp.
 * 
 * The typical worflow is as follows:
 *
 *
 * @code
 * int main()
 * {
 *     auto eventManager = std::make_shared<Core::EventManager>();
 *     Core::ServiceManager serviceManager(eventManager);
 *     serviceManager.registerService<SensorService>(...);
 *     serviceManager.registerService<LoggerService>(...);
 *     runUiLoop();   // blocks until user exits
 *     // shutdown happens below
 * }
 *  // For tests
 *  auto& w = sm.get<WifiService>(ServiceId::Wifi);
 * @endcode
 */
